/**
\fn undefined SpriteLayer::deserialize(Deserializer deserializer)
\brief Restore Layer state or apply an incremental update.
\param deserializer Reader positioned at a record written by SpriteLayer::serialize().
An initial record restores sprites, independent/authored Parts, shared artwork, order, transforms and active
state into an empty or populated Layer. Loading validates records and resources
before replacing the existing collection, including mount endpoint, cycle and
duplicate-owner checks. Old sprites retained by script are
detached; new bodies join the destination solver after validation. Tween channels
are rebound to the destination Layer, including zoom.

The Layer keeps its Port, application event handlers and caller-selected
serialization flags. Its saved identities and state replace their previous values.
A record/resource validation error leaves the existing Layer collection and state
intact; discard the failed reader. Incremental updates modify existing sprites and
require matching identities/order. They are not staged scene replacement.

\note Call outside animation modifiers and a physics solve. The shared physical
world is not recreated; configure its gravity and damping in the application.
\sa SpriteLayer::serialize(), SpriteLayer::setSerializationFlags()
*/
